{
  "info": {
    "name": "Prafi API",
    "description": "Backend API (Express + Sequelize + PostgreSQL).\n\n**Setup (once)**\n1. Import this collection and `Prafi-Local.postman_environment.json`.\n2. Select **Prafi Local** in the environment dropdown (top right).\n3. In **Prafi Local**, set `superadminPassword` (same as SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD in .env) in the **Current value** column, then Ctrl+S.\n\n**Automatic saving**: after every Login, the token is saved to the environment as `{{token}}` (last logged-in user) and `{{superadminToken}}` / `{{adminToken}}` / `{{tenantToken}}`. Register and Upload save `adminEmail`, `tenantEmail`, `imageId`, `imageUrl`. Each save is printed in the Postman Console. Scripts write the environment **Current value** (Initial value stays empty on purpose).\n\n**Collection Runner**: turn on *Keep variable values* (Persist responses / variables) so values from the run stay in the environment afterwards.\n\n**Roles**: superadmin → can create admin, admin → can create tenant.\n\n**Responses**: `{ success: true, data }` or `{ success: false, error: { code, message, details? } }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000"
    },
    {
      "key": "superadminEmail",
      "value": "admin@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "superadminPassword",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Same as SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD in .env"
    },
    {
      "key": "newUserPassword",
      "value": "Secret123!",
      "description": "Password given to users created by the Register requests"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "var save = (key, value) => { pm.environment.set(key, value); pm.collectionVariables.set(key, value); console.log('saved {{' + key + '}}'); };",
          "var body = null;",
          "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { /* not JSON, e.g. an image */ }",
          "",
          "if (body) pm.test('Response is JSON with a success flag', () => pm.expect(body).to.have.property('success'));",
          "",
          "// Any login response: keep the token for that role + as {{token}} (the last logged-in user)",
          "if (body && body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
          "  save('token', body.data.accessToken);",
          "  save(body.data.user.role + 'Token', body.data.accessToken);",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Public. Returns `{ status: 'ok' }` when the server is running."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "description": "Login and create an admin.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login - Superadmin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{superadminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{superadminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Returns `accessToken` (JWT) and the user. The token is saved to `{{superadminToken}}`. Also saved to `{{token}}` (the last logged-in user)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - Admin (by Superadmin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{superadminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Andi\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Wijaya\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"081234567890\",\n  \"email\": \"admin{{$timestamp}}@prafi.test\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newUserPassword}}\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires **superadmin** token. A superadmin can only create `admin` accounts.\n\nBody: `firstName`, `lastName`, `phoneNumber`, `email`, `password` (min 8), `role` — all required. `faceImageId` optional (id from **Images / Upload Image**).\n\nErrors: 400 validation, 401 no/invalid token, 403 role not allowed, 409 email or faceImageId already used."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "var save = (key, value) => { pm.environment.set(key, value); pm.collectionVariables.set(key, value); console.log('saved {{' + key + '}}'); };",
                  "var data = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (data) save('adminEmail', data.email);",
                  "pm.test('Password is not returned', () => pm.expect(data).to.not.have.property('password'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - Admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newUserPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs in as the admin created above. The token is saved to `{{adminToken}}`. Also saved to `{{token}}` (the last logged-in user)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Images",
      "description": "Upload an image first; its id is used as faceImageId when registering a user.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Upload Image",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "sample-face.png",
                  "description": "jpg / png / webp / gif, max 5 MB"
                },
                {
                  "key": "altText",
                  "value": "Face photo",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Optional, defaults to the file name"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/images",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "images"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Any logged-in user. Multipart field `image` (max 5 MB, jpg/png/webp/gif) + optional `altText`.\n\nThe returned `id` is saved to `{{imageId}}` (used by *Register - Tenant*), `url` to `{{imageUrl}}`.\n\n**In Postman desktop:** re-select the file in the `image` row (Postman can't store local file paths across machines) — a sample is in `postman/sample-face.png`.\n\nErrors: 400 missing/wrong file type, 413 file larger than 5 MB."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "var save = (key, value) => { pm.environment.set(key, value); pm.collectionVariables.set(key, value); console.log('saved {{' + key + '}}'); };",
                  "var data = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (data) { save('imageId', data.id); save('imageUrl', data.url); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Open Image (public link)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{imageUrl}}",
              "host": [
                "{{imageUrl}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public, no token. This is the link the frontend puts in `<img src>` — e.g. `http://localhost:4000/images/<file>.png`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Is an image', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.match(/^image\\//));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Users",
      "description": "Register a tenant with the uploaded face image, then log in as that tenant.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register - Tenant with face image (by Admin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Budi\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Santoso\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"08123456789\",\n  \"email\": \"tenant{{$timestamp}}@prafi.test\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newUserPassword}}\",\n  \"role\": \"tenant\",\n  \"faceImageId\": {{imageId}}\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires **admin** token. An admin can only create `tenant` accounts.\n\nRun **Images / Upload Image** first — its `id` is saved to `{{imageId}}` and used as `faceImageId` here. Each image can belong to only one user (409 otherwise)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "var save = (key, value) => { pm.environment.set(key, value); pm.collectionVariables.set(key, value); console.log('saved {{' + key + '}}'); };",
                  "var data = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (data) save('tenantEmail', data.email);",
                  "pm.test('Face image is linked', () => pm.expect(data.faceImage.url).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - Tenant",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{tenantEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newUserPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs in as the tenant created above. The token is saved to `{{tenantToken}}`. Also saved to `{{token}}` (the last logged-in user)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (current user)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Any logged-in user. Uses `{{token}}` = whoever logged in last, so run any Login request first. Returns the profile including `faceImage` (with its full `url`)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Me",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Budiman\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Susanto\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"08999999999\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Any logged-in user updates **their own** account (uses `{{token}}` = whoever logged in last). There is no id in the URL, so nobody can update another user.\n\nSend only the fields to change:\n- `firstName`, `lastName`, `phoneNumber`, `email` (non-empty strings; email must be unique)\n- `faceImageId`: id from **Upload Image**, or `null` to remove it (each image belongs to one user)\n- `password` (min 8) **together with** `currentPassword`\n\nNot allowed (400): `id`, `role`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, unknown fields, empty body.\n\nErrors: 400 validation / wrong currentPassword, 401 no token, 409 email or faceImageId used by another user.\n\n**Changing your password here does not update `{{newUserPassword}}`**, so the Login requests for this user will fail until you change it back or update that variable."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List Users",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "description": "1-100"
                },
                {
                  "key": "role",
                  "value": "tenant",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Optional filter; must be a role you are allowed to see"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "One route, result depends on who calls it (uses `{{token}}` = whoever logged in last):\n\n- **superadmin** → all accounts (superadmin, admin, tenant)\n- **admin** → tenant accounts only\n- **tenant** → 403 (tenants only have **Me**)\n\nQuery: `page` (default 1), `limit` (default 20, max 100), `role` (optional filter). Response: `data` = users (with `faceImage`), `meta` = `{ page, limit, total, totalPages }`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.test('Returns a list with paging meta', () => { pm.expect(body.data).to.be.an('array'); pm.expect(body.meta).to.have.property('total'); });",
                  "  pm.test('No passwords returned', () => body.data.forEach((u) => pm.expect(u).to.not.have.property('password')));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('Tenant gets 403', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(403));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Examples (role check)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Admin Ping (superadmin, admin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ping",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "ping"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Allowed: superadmin, admin. A tenant token returns 403."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Tenant Ping (all roles)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{tenantToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tenant/ping",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tenant",
                "ping"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Allowed: superadmin, admin, tenant."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Cleanup",
      "description": "Deletes the uploaded image (the tenant keeps existing with faceImageId = null).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Delete Image",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{tenantToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/images/:id",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "images",
                ":id"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{imageId}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires **tenant** role (current rule in `image.routes.ts`). Deletes the DB row and the file. Users using this image get `faceImageId = null`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
